[31m-## Mental model[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Python is dynamically executed but can be developed with strong discipline through type hints, static analysis, tests, immutable conventions, small modules, and explicit contracts.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Key differences to internalize[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Indentation is syntax.[m
[31m-- Type hints are not runtime enforcement unless a library validates them.[m
[31m-- `None` is the null value and optionality should be explicit.[m
[31m-- Iterables, generators, comprehensions, and context managers are central idioms.[m
[31m-- Exceptions are commonly used for error propagation, but public boundaries should map them intentionally.[m
[31m-- Virtual environments isolate project dependencies.[m
[31m-- Modules and packages replace assembly/namespace expectations in different ways.[m
[31m-- Duck typing is common, but protocols and abstract base classes can express interfaces.[m
[31m-- Dataclasses and Pydantic models serve different purposes.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Quality tools selected[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Ruff: formatting-compatible linting and import/order checks.[m
[31m-- mypy strict mode: catches missing and inconsistent type assumptions.[m
[31m-- pytest: concise deterministic tests and fixtures.[m
[31m-- Pydantic: runtime validation at external boundaries.[m
[31m-[m
